nload/0.15.0/native-appcast-macos-x86_64.xml"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy/releases/assets/703905334","id":703905334,"node_id":"RA_kwDOFoAj8s4p9L42","name":"native-appcast-windows-x86_64.xml","label":"","uploader":{"login":"appflowy","id":86001920,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg2MDAxOTIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/86001920?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy","html_url":"https://github.com/appflowy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/appflowy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/xml","state":"uploaded","size":774,"digest":"sha256:3e26d36cc446396b09d46daef4a7d1af3055eebeb137874665f2b43c4affa187","download_count":13,"created_at":"2026-11-03T01:59:44Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T01:59:44Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy/releases/download/0.15.0/native-appcast-windows-x86_64.xml"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy/tarball/0.15.0","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy/zipball/0.15.0","body":"### 🚀 v0.15.0\r\n\r\n#### New Features\r\n\r\n- **Dashboards** — Added dashboards combining views from multiple databases, with movable and resizable widgets, shared filters, and personal filter changes. Local dashboards could reuse existing views; creating new widget views required a server connection.\r\n- **Charts and drill-downs** — Added Number charts for workspaces with Pro features, expanded grouping and display controls, and drill-down tables for exploring a chart's records and saving the result as a filtered view.\r\n- **Page widths** — Added full-width and custom-width formatting per document, shared with collaborators while retaining each user's default for pages without an explicit width.\r\n- **Image search results** — Showed the image and matched text behind a search result, and opened documents at the matched image when the server supplied this information.\r\n- **Native update installation** — Added user-initiated installation on macOS and Windows x64 when the server enabled it and supplied a signed update feed. Retained manual downloads when native installation was unavailable.\r\n\r\n#### Improvements\r\n\r\n- **Database exports** — Added A4, A3, Letter, and Legal paper sizes with portrait or landscape orientation. Paginated wide PDF tables at a readable size and exported the active view's visible fields and current rows, with support for complete offline caches.\r\n- **Board views** — Added sorting within columns, column calculations, and backgrounds based on group colors.\r\n- **Images** — Saved thumbnails and decoded images at their display size across documents and database cards, reducing the size of images held in memory.\r\n- **Translations** — Updated interface translations and corrected Grid header and cell alignment in right-to-left languages.\r\n\r\n#### Bug Fixes\r\n\r\n- Preserved individual heading text during multi-block conversion, kept link formatting when editing URLs, and allowed read-only toggle blocks to expand without changing the shared document.\r\n- Prevented moving subpages in the sidebar from sending them to Trash, and preserved external-link and date mentions when copying or exporting document text.\r\n- Corrected row peek navigation and calendar row opening, focused newly added Grid rows for editing, and kept hidden Board groups usable during partial schema refreshes.\r\n- Preserved document image sizes while scrolling and recovered missing or damaged media caches without losing image authentication.\r\n- Prevented duplicated database content from uploading before its page was acknowledged by the server, and preserved database layouts when reopening views.\r\n- Fixed PDF image reading with Ollama models that advertised vision support through their capabilities.\r\n\r\n#### ⚠️ Action Required\r\n\r\n- Self-hosted workspaces still require **AppFlowy Cloud v0.19.10 or later**.\r\n- Self-hosted dashboards require server support for the Dashboard layout. Before using more than twelve widgets or four widgets in one row, deploy the updated dashboard validation to every realtime server.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AppFlowy-IO/AppFlowy/releases/429745918/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0}}